# phi-agent — local, non-repository configuration.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/phi-agent/env and edit. phi-agent-contain SOURCES this
# file as a shell fragment: one `KEY=value` per line, no `export`, no logic —
# but shell rules apply, so quote any value that contains a space
# ("like this") and `$HOME` / `~` expand.
#
# NOTHING SECRET GOES HERE. The provider API key is held by the brokering
# service outside the containment and is read from its own file. This file
# only carries paths and identity. pi's own process environment (PI_OFFLINE
# and friends) is a separate, repo-shipped file: ~/.config/phi-agent/pi/env.

# --- coding profile ---
#
# No fixed "code root". Open the coding agent in any directory:
# `phi agent code ~/dev/some-project`. That directory is the ONLY thing
# under $HOME the session can see. A configurable blocklist
# (~/.config/phi-agent/code-blocklist, copy it from code-blocklist.example)
# guards the picker; it is not the security boundary.

# Toolchain cache dedicated to coding, kept separate from your own.
#PHI_AGENT_A2_TOOLCHAIN_CACHE=$HOME/.cache/phi-agent/coding/toolchains

# Git identity for coding's local commits. Coding never mounts your
# ~/.gitconfig. Quoted: the value has a space (see the sourcing note above).
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="phi agent"
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=phi-agent@localhost
